    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2K75PqDBtCa033REVvmuGz-4rlD6tLa7Dm6qjY8rTT8.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\nIn a series LCR circuit, the rms voltage across the resistor and the capacitor are 30 V and 90 V respectively. If the applied voltage is $50 \\sqrt{2} \\sin \\omega t$, then the peak voltage across the inductor is",
